"record_id":"MLDB-000385","detection":"ICP-MS","method_description":"Lipophilicity was presented as log Po/w values, which were determined by the flask-shaking method [46]. An aliquot of a stock solution of the ruthenium complex in water (saturated with octanol) was added to an equal volume of octanol (saturated with water), and the mixture was shaken overnight at 60 rpm to allow partitioning at 298 K. After the sample was centrifuged at 3000 rpm for 15 min, the aqueous layer was carefully separated from the octanol layer for ruthenium analysis. The Ru concentration in the aqueous phase was determined by ICP-MS (Thermal) and used to calculate the [Ru]o/[Ru]w ratio."}]}